        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dd34b110-3cb4-572e-ba83-7448a46278ee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jane Mayer, Charles Koch, David Koch, the Koch family\n- Organizations: Koch Industries, Citizens United\n- Products: Dark Money: The Hidden History of the Billionaires Behind the Rise of the Radical Right\n- Concepts: conservative libertarians, political influence in the United States\n\nFacts:\n- Citizens United is a conservative 501(c)(4) non-profit organization in the United States that was started in 1988 with major funding from the billionaire Koch family.\n- In 2013, Koch Industries was the second-largest privately owned company in the United States, with revenues of $115 billion, and the Koch family controlled it.\n- In 2016, American investigative journalist Jane Mayer wrote the non-fiction book Dark Money: The Hidden History of the Billionaires Behind the Rise of the Radical Right.\n- Dark Money says that a network of extremely wealthy conservative libertarians, especially Charles Koch and David Koch, funded organizations that worked together to influence academic institutions, think tanks, the courts, statehouses, Congress, and the American presidency for their own benefit.\n- The Koch family is an American family engaged in business and is especially noted for its political activities.",
